        # (github.com/project-barry/pb-os, external-and-mods/kernel-sm8650/sm8550, at 8ea4653; each one's
        # header says what of it is ours and where it was tried: on a Thor for 0620, 0630 and 0560 (ours
        # rebased onto Armada's FastRPC context-leak fix, lore v3 by Anandu Krishnan E), on a
        # Retroid Pocket Nova for 0545 (not yet on a Thor), 0546 and 0505's wake, on a KONKR Pocket FIT
        # for 0547): the battery firmware's own charge switches (ClamShell's CLAMSHELL_CHARGE_LIMIT=
        # firmware), the bottom panel's brightness, the bottom touchscreen's lost contacts, the battery's
        # power, FastRPC to the ADSP's sensor hub (the motion sensors), deep sleep's wake by a charger
        # and no battery notifications while asleep (0505 changes deep sleep only; 0547 any sleep); and
        # GEM's fault handler honouring the mmap offset, for Turnip's dma-buf mappings at an offset
        # (0611, at 55c2d28f76, tried on a Retroid Pocket 6, not yet on a Thor).
        # thor-*: the body's motor as an LRA (PB-OS's device tree lines, tried on a Thor), the gamepad
        # MCU's joystick frame settable, the sensor hub's process types and PDR (PB-OS's), FastRPC's legacy
        # mappings refused without a session. (The top panel's frame length calibrated per unit,
        # ROCKNIX's, is Armada's 0518 since their 664da8c; it was our thor-0005.) rocknix-*: ROCKNIX's
        # (ROCKNIX/distribution, packages/linux/patches/7.2): the panels held in reset while the display
        # clocks are handed over at boot, so the bootloader's splash doesn't glitch (0017, at 86d6ef9c76,
        # PR #3495, tried on a Thor); QSEED4's horizontal preload of 7 behind the inline rotator, so a
        # rotated layer split over two pipes (a game's buffer shown directly, turned for the sideways
        # panels) has no seam (0018, at 8662e9f5ad, measured on an SM8650 tablet, not yet tried on a Thor).
        # stable-*: fixes of Linux's 7.2 stable releases after Armada's 7.2.6, as they are there
        # (each one's header names its release and upstream commit): 7.2.8's to DisplayPort and the
        # DPU (0001..0003: Armada's kernel hard-freezes the Thor when a DP monitor is plugged in,
        # Armada #529; PB-OS's on 7.2.8 shows DP working); hibernation's image preallocated before
        # the kernel threads freeze (0004, 7.2.9); GPU fences outliving their ring or VM, and the
        # GPU's runtime PM on unbind (0005, 0006, 7.2.8); hci_qca's remove after a failed open
        # (0007, 7.2.8); UCSI's glink remove and its DisplayPort entry (0008, 0009, 7.2.10); the
        # GENI serial engines' QUP core clock vote (0010, 7.2.10); ath12k's panic handler reverted
        # (0011, 7.2.11); arm64 hibernation's resume with the runtime linear map and EL2's vectors
        # set again (0012, 0013, 7.2.8); the WSA macro's volume written once its clocks run (0014,
        # 7.2.10). Not yet tried on a Thor.
        # upstream-*: fixes in mainline Linux 7.4, as they are there (each one's header names its
        # commit): q6apm's PCM position at the end of the ring and after a prepare, and its DSP
        # buffer mappings: the unmap's reply, the position buffer's handle, unmapped before the
        # topology goes, callbacks before probe's data (0001..0006); the battery firmware's USB type
        # from USB_ADAP_TYPE (0007); pmic_glink's altmode worker kept until the devices resume
        # (0008); DP link training's failure reported after a last reinit, HPD state changed under
        # its lock (0009, 0010). Not yet tried on a Thor.
        # sap-*: SteamOS-ARM-Port's (github.com/hashtagbasit/SteamOS-ARM-Port,
        # external-and-mods/kernel-sm8550/patches, at 4f1892e, not upstream): the VM close's fence
        # wait bounded at 3 s (0009, seen there on a Thor). Not yet tried on our kernel.
        # armada-*: Armada's, from after our 664da8c (their numbers; applied after ours, not in
        # their series' place): a plane's colorops kept across suspend (0077a); -EINVAL for a plane
        # layout with no free pipe (0077b); GPU interrupts nothing handles masked when they fire
        # (1115); the PMIC haptics SoundWire port's clock stop handshake skipped (0570). Not yet
        # tried on a Thor.
